#
# Conformance case: teleology/resource-exhaustion-gates-action.
#
# An action schema declares a logic:actionResource (buildLock). The probed state SUPPLIES
# the resource (logic:resourceSupply) but it is flagged logic:resourceExhausted "true",
# so the resource is unavailable: the gate verdict is logic:GateDenied with a reason
# naming the unavailable resource and the schema's compensation. This is the
# representation-level resource facet (the seam to logic:competesForResource), NOT a real
# build engine-lock.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/resource-exhaustion-gates-action/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
